From c4a260e5c0fa59ac712cf7e318b40e74fa8dd6fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:44:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/54] drm/gma500: add hardware fences for sgxfive contexts

Give each transfer context a dma_fence timeline and a list of pending fences.
The firmware writes a finished job's number to the context's fence word
before it raises SW_EVENT, so the interrupt handler now signals every
context's fences up to that number; a context going away fails what is
left. KUnit checks the sequence-number comparison, including across the
32-bit wrap.

Assisted-by: LLM
